{"title":"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> call a finite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/5/595bc07c1d3bb62a23791361010c1409f3066973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1, a_2 \\ldots a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> of positive integers <i>progressive</i> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc2d3fe323f662034210558950f89c84c88f9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &lt; a_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac5179cf12e1a7ff085b57db0ca3f9d9c2e6e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff83105557fa452974107ed1f164b322e4fe8fd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />. Find the number of progressive sequences such that the sum of the terms in the sequence is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62a47cbc153efdf4611d8660429ea879be3f192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then dividing through by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we see that we can find the number of progressive sequences whose sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaaf5b1f81e05b909e6966235fa22e53f36b9cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360}{x} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" />, and whose first term is not 1. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b638d9d94daf2e12c2f476e46b317d70394ec00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the number of progressive sequences whose sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and whose first term is not 1, then we can express the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e3c64638c1eb50ee3809ae7668f7baad6e63632.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}N &amp;= a(359) + a(179) + a(119) + a(89) + a(71) + a(59) + a(44) + a(39) \\\\ &amp;+ a(35) + a(29) + a(23) + a(19) + a(17) + a(14) + a(11) + a(9) \\\\ &amp;+ a(8) + a(7) + a(5) + a(4) + a(3) + a(2) + a(1) + 1 \\end{align*}\" width=\"556\" height=\"68\" />\n</p><p>And in general, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10c2cee0997a13dfff9fe9c71321114b0272cd6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(k) = 1+\\sum_{d|k\\text{ and } d\\ne 1,k}a(d-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -27px\" width=\"242\" height=\"47\" />.\n</p><p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/1178af8fcc5f3f3acb9f151f7dcc2c4eefe88fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> at the end accounts for the sequence whose only term is 360. Fortunately, many of these numbers are prime; we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e30e1c92d78943a6a7ba62a056829ac88299eba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(p) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> for primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> as the only such sequence is \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />\" itself. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e90184d429d1aa064bd5233b2b91b9a8ccee0b7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. So we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/939d04b54ac6c6ce2171c8a055c8b5f671603e83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = 15 + a(119) + a(44) + a(39) + a(35) + a(14) + a(9) + a(8) + a(4)\\]\" width=\"487\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>For small <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b638d9d94daf2e12c2f476e46b317d70394ec00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is easy to compute: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad38542c2eaadb7fa4b51251dcb98ada20974383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(4) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/d/27d13a9ea657e7bf1e7baab168e0f2b981fdf7fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(8) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439fe35d0ef8ca638a6df3003536806cc1d9adc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(9) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. For intermediate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c766eb3dc70002f4a99585da72b40f97136fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> below), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b638d9d94daf2e12c2f476e46b317d70394ec00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> can be computed recursively using previously-computed values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bde323d495532f7ac8025b9cf75eafea70f9eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(\\cdot)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />, similar to dynamic programming. Then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373072aae70313c8f8987969d5e11dd12946f6c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a(14) &amp;= 1+a(6) = 1+2 = 3\\\\ a(35) &amp;= 1+a(6)+a(4) = 1 + 2 + 1 = 4 \\\\ a(39) &amp;= 2 + a(12) = 2+4 = 6 \\\\ a(44) &amp;= 2 + a(21) + a(10) = 2+4+2=8 \\\\ a(119) &amp;= 1 + a(16) + a(6) = 1 + 3 + 2 = 6 \\end{align*}\" width=\"341\" height=\"117\" />\nThus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/91615b1165658eccfd72645e6197c4bd86c25f4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 15+6+8+6+4+3+2+2+1 = \\boxed{047}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"373\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-scrabbler94\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/T-8-B-XgiiI\">https://youtu.be/T-8-B-XgiiI</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Zfi2AVq6ak\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Zfi2AVq6ak</a> ~ MathEx\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II\" title=\"2019 AIME II\">2019 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017182913\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 241/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6156/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.038      1 -total\n 59.47%    7.754      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.55%    5.026      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17422:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017182913 and revision id 260761. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}